PROJECT: UNIQUE RESTAURANT — PROFESSIONAL NIGERIAN RESTAURANT WEBSITE

1. ROLE

Act as a senior full-stack web developer, professional UI/UX designer, restaurant website specialist, and database architect with extensive experience building modern, responsive, conversion-focused restaurant websites.

Your task is to design and develop a complete, professional, visually appealing, and fully functional multi-page website for a Nigerian food business called Unique Restaurant.

The website must have a premium restaurant feel, excellent user experience, intuitive navigation, and a well-structured backend that allows the restaurant owner to manage the website without needing programming knowledge.

Do not create a generic food website. Build a distinctive digital identity that communicates the quality, deliciousness, authenticity, and richness of Nigerian cuisine.

2. BUSINESS INFORMATION

Business Name: Unique Restaurant

Business Category: Nigerian Restaurant / Food Business

Location: Owo Ede, Osogbo, Osun State, Nigeria.

Target Market: Nigerians, particularly residents of Osogbo and surrounding communities, students, workers, families, visitors, and anyone interested in delicious Nigerian meals.

Business Description:

Unique Restaurant specializes in preparing and serving delicious, freshly prepared Nigerian meals. The restaurant offers a variety of traditional Nigerian dishes, including rice meals, beans, local delicacies, soups, swallows, and other popular Nigerian foods.

The website should communicate freshness, affordability, quality, excellent food preparation, and a welcoming restaurant experience.

Brand Colours:

Primary Red: Used for important brand elements, buttons, and highlights.

Black: Used for strong typography, navigation, and premium visual contrast.

Orange: Used for food-related highlights, accents, and call-to-action elements.

White: Used as the primary background colour to maintain cleanliness and readability.

Use these colours consistently throughout the website. Avoid excessive colour combinations.

3. AUDIENCE

Design the website primarily for Nigerians.

The average visitor should be able to:

Understand what Unique Restaurant offers immediately.

Browse available Nigerian meals.

See food pictures, descriptions, and prices in Nigerian Naira (₦).

Select a meal they want to purchase.

Fill in their order and delivery information.

Place an order directly through WhatsApp.

Find the restaurant's location and contact information.

The website must be easy to use, even for visitors who are not particularly familiar with technology.

4. PROJECT GOAL

Build a professional restaurant website that serves as Unique Restaurant's digital storefront.

The website should achieve the following:

Establish a strong and recognizable online presence.

Showcase Nigerian meals through attractive food photography.

Make it easy for customers to discover available meals and prices.

Generate food orders through WhatsApp.

Give the restaurant owner complete control over food listings and website content through an admin dashboard.

Provide a seamless experience on mobile phones, tablets, and desktop computers.

Connect to Supabase for database storage and management.

Be properly structured and optimized for deployment on Vercel.

