12. VERCEL DEPLOYMENT REQUIREMENTS

The website will be deployed on Vercel.

Build the application with deployment readiness in mind from the beginning.

Requirements:

Ensure all packages and dependencies are properly configured.

Use environment variables for all sensitive configuration.

Create a valid production build script.

Configure Vercel rewrites or SPA fallback routing so refreshing /about, /menu, /contact, and /admin/login does not produce a 404 error.

Ensure image paths and assets resolve correctly after deployment.

Avoid hardcoded localhost URLs.

Avoid server-side dependencies that are incompatible with the deployment environment.

Do not expose Supabase service role credentials.

Ensure protected routes work after deployment.

Test all forms and Supabase operations in production configuration.

Check for TypeScript errors and build errors before deployment.

Ensure the application does not depend on local development files or machine-specific paths.

Create a .env.example file containing:

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

Use the correct public Supabase publishable/anon key according to the configured Supabase project.

Any privileged server-side credentials must remain server-side and must never use a VITE_ prefix.

Include clear instructions for adding the environment variables to Vercel.

