15. DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTIONS

Build the website progressively, but maintain a consistent architecture throughout.

Do not sacrifice functionality for appearance.

Do not create static dashboard screens that merely look functional.

Do not use fake authentication.

Do not hardcode menu data into components when it should come from Supabase.

Do not use insecure frontend-only database permissions.

Do not leave essential functionality as TODO comments.

Do not generate unnecessary pages outside the requested scope.

If any Supabase credentials are unavailable, build the integration layer properly, create the database SQL scripts, and clearly identify the credentials needed to complete the connection.

